WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.620
Mark Ruffalo's Hulk will smash again in the
MCU.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.920
At least that's the word coming from the folks
at The Illuminerdi, as the site is claiming

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.769
that "sources" close to Disney+ and Marvel's
upcoming She-Hulk series have provided "definitive"

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:16.520
proof that Ruffalo is officially on board
to reprise his role as Bruce Banner on the

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.320
small screen.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.439
A kick-ass, new hero and a returning fan favorite?

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.620
"Best of both worlds."

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.340
It should be noted, of course, that the site
does not provide said proof for the masses

00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:30.400
to see, nor do they actually say what that
proof is; one would have to imagine they've

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.850
seen Ruffalo's signature on an actual contract
for it to count as "definitive."

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.219
Either way, it still might be wise for MCU
enthusiasts to temper their excitement about

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.040
Hulk's return until Team Marvel makes their
own announcement.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.440
That news would hardly come a shock, though,
as it's been widely rumored in recent weeks

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:49.590
that Ruffalo's big green guy would indeed
be joining the anxiously-anticipated She-Hulk

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:50.080
series.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.340
ScreenRant reports that Ruffalo himself even
recently confirmed that he was in talks with

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:58.540
Marvel and Disney to reprise his role as Banner-slash-Hulk
for the Disney+ series.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.070
Seems those talks might have been a bit further
along than Ruffalo was letting on, as The

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:07.220
Illuminerdi is now reporting the actor's deal
was likely already in place when he made those

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:07.720
comments.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.140
There's still no confirmation as to how many
episodes of She-Hulk Ruffalo might appear

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:16.200
in, or if his new deal with Marvel might include
another big screen turn in the future, but

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.430
whatever the case, we're just psyched to see
Ruffalo's Hulk on screen again in any capacity.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:24.360
If you recall, Mark Ruffalo took over the
role of Hulk after the folks at Marvel famously

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.590
parted ways with O.G.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.340
MCU Hulk Edward Norton.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.760
Making his first appearance in 2012's The
Avengers, Ruffalo immediately made the role

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:32.260
his own.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.760
"Now might be a really good time for you to
get angry."

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.640
"That's my secret, Cap.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:40.620
I'm always angry."

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:45.100
He continued to play Bruce Banner and Hulk
in four subsequent MCU flicks, not including

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.980
uncredited cameo appearances.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.180
Marvel's brass are clearly fans, and have
now reportedly ensured that no other actor

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.900
will play Hulk for the foreseeable future.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.760
As for what role Bruce Banner will play in
She-Hulk, if the Disney+ series stays true

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.760
to the character's comic book origins, his
role could be fairly major.

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:05.520
For those unfamiliar with She-Hulk, the character's
name is Jennifer Walters, and she's a successful

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.620
attorney, often for the superhero set.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.300
She also just so happens to be Bruce Banner's
cousin.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.459
If you're wondering how Walters becomes She-Hulk,
the transformation occurs after she receives

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:18.780
a blood transfusion from dear cousin Bruce,
after which she finds herself with a similar

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.280
green affliction, although she actually Hulks
out with her intellect and self-control intact.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.240
"How's this, hot stuff?"

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.120
Walters eventually becomes a member of the
Avengers and A-Force, and she continues to

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.400
play a major role in Marvel comics, so you
can likely expect to see a lot more of the

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.960
character as the MCU charges ahead.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:46.200
As for what that could entail, well, Marvel
Studios would be remiss not to use Walters'

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.770
career as an attorney, a 7-foot, green attorney,
that is, as a way to introduce her to the

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.680
wider MCU.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.790
The studio's head honcho, Kevin Feige, has
already made it quite clear that characters

00:02:55.790 --> 00:03:00.780
introduced via Disney+ series will be making
appearances in future films, and we can think

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.810
of a hero or two who may be in need of legal
representation in the very near future.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.999
Case in point: Peter Parker, who was just
publicly outed as Spider-Man and framed for

00:03:08.999 --> 00:03:12.849
an extremely high-profile murder, and who
suddenly has some blowhard named J. Jonah

00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:14.960
Jameson ranting about what a menace he is.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:20.640
"Spider-Man: A Psychopath wielding powers
he has no right to possess, trying to pass

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.280
himself off as a hero.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:23.420
You're
no hero!"

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:27.590
As for Banner, well, for all we know, his
stint on She-Hulk could be a one-off deal

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:31.909
that sees him supplying the necessary Hulk
blood to facilitate his cousin's transformation,

00:03:31.909 --> 00:03:33.460
and going on his merry green way.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.700
We're not-so-secretly hoping, though, that
this news means that Ruffalo still has a vital

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.900
role to play in future phases of the MCU.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.739
She-Hulk has not yet received an official
release date, but production on the series

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:47.430
is expected to begin in July; we'll keep an
eye out for an official announcement, and

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.040
we'll be sure to keep you informed.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:50.540
"Hulk out!"

